🧪 Broken Brute-Force Protection (IP Block)
🎯 Objective
Brute-force the password of user carlos by exploiting flawed brute-force protection logic, then access his account.


🔍 Vulnerability Summary
The application implements IP-based brute-force protection, blocking login attempts after 3 failed tries.
However, there is a logic flaw:
The failed login counter resets when a valid login occurs.
This allows an attacker to bypass the limit by alternating between:
A valid login (attacker account)
A brute-force attempt (victim account)

⚠️ Impact

Attackers can perform unlimited password attempts
Protection mechanism becomes ineffective
Leads to account takeover


